    },
    "body": "References #434 #245 #421. The de-banding payoff test: **ARM BF (full-width retrieval anchor supply) free top-1 8.17% vs banded ARM B 7.64% (+0.54pp), vs nulls 2.14/3.09; anchor accuracy 11.4% vs 9.3% (+2.1pp). All three pre-declared conditions PASS — de-banding pays.** Honest read: the 3.8× retrieval-MRR gain converts to a modest anchor gain — retrieval quality is no longer the binding constraint on anchor supply; the continuation side-table is. Decision (Casey, C→A): **de-banding ADOPTED** as an implementation item — consumer audit of band-sparsity assumptions first, then full-width storage in the #245 path; priority moderate (the case = 3.8× raw retrieval + measured anchor gain).",
    "closed_by": {
